  "readmeFile": "nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.3.1\n\n* Fixed: IOExtensions.UnifyPathSeperator collapsed the leading \\\\ of a UNC path, so\n  \\\\server\\share\\file became \\server\\share\\file, which Windows resolves against the current\n  drive (C:\\server\\share\\file). On Windows the run of separators at the start of a path is now\n  reduced to exactly two instead of one, so //server/share/file becomes \\\\server\\share\\file and\n  \\\\?\\ and \\\\.\\ device paths survive. Nothing changes on Linux or macOS.\n  If you pass caller-supplied relative paths through it before Path.Combine, a value starting\n  with // or \\\\ now comes back as a UNC path to another machine. Strip leading separators first.\n\nUpgrading from 10.2.x or earlier? 10.3.0 changed how Com.H.Shell and Com.H.Pdf behave, which\nmatters if you run external commands or convert HTML to PDF. Its notes list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
